{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788666228816165001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"complex-sassy-blackfly","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"c506492e0254e3b92e25e8624f9093ac68ef8d99cd48a0063f30e5d9ece3a7d2","event_uuid":"34dda3c2-28d3-4c4f-9d85-d1ac137e9511","position":{"commit_sha":"6f56d9fbf1cb55e31aba8521944162a80a5662c1","position":"1788654045640987001-34dda3c2-28d3-4c4f-9d85-d1ac137e9511"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"19b222b88a887ec73ad92e096ff198e0ec2e5e30a82a71f9cd0975533e78be36","event_uuid":"3e3d48a6-51e3-420d-b082-f247e88c7fc3","position":{"commit_sha":"1c17aedeb626940f97f02784dea2d149bd75f8fa","position":"1788662864776870001-3e3d48a6-51e3-420d-b082-f247e88c7fc3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## RECURRENCE — and this time the root cause is identified, not just the symptom\n\nreview-bot went down again and stayed down ~59 minutes, silently. I restored it manually. But the\nimportant part is *why* it did not come back on its own, which this ticket previously did not have.\n\n### Root cause: `unless-stopped` plus a clean exit is a permanent outage\n\n```\ndocker inspect -f '{{.HostConfig.RestartPolicy.Name}}':\n  compose-review-bot-1   unless-stopped\n  compose-opcert-1       unless-stopped\n  compose-gerrit-1       unless-stopped\n\ndocker ps -a  (before my intervention):\n  compose-review-bot-1 | Exited (0) 59 minutes ago      <-- clean exit, code 0\n  rebar-mcp-...        | Up About a minute (healthy)\n  compose-opcert-1     | Up About a minute\n  compose-gerrit-1     | Up About a minute\n```\n\n`unless-stopped` means \"restart it unless it was **explicitly stopped**.\" review-bot exited with\n**code 0** — a clean, voluntary exit — and Docker therefore treated it as intentionally stopped and\ndeclined to restart it, including across the host reboot that brought every other container back.\n\nSo this is not a flaky container or a crash loop. It is a policy that is *correct* for a service a\nhuman stops on purpose, and *wrong* for a service whose absence silently disables the merge gate.\nThe other three containers came back precisely because they had not exited cleanly first.\n\n**Consequence, stated plainly: with review-bot down there is no source of `LLM-Review` votes, so no\nchange can satisfy the two-vote gate and nothing can merge.** For 59 minutes the project's merge path\nwas closed and nothing said so.\n\n### The reboot was deliberate and external — not a crash\n\nWorth recording so this is not misfiled as instability:\n\n```\nSep 06 02:40:41 systemd-logind: Power key pressed short.\nSep 06 02:40:42 systemd-logind: Powering off...\nSep 06 02:41:11 systemd-logind: Failed to get load state of poweroff.target: Connection timed out\nSep 06 02:41:12 systemd-logind: Failed to execute poweroff operation: Connection timed out\nSep 06 02:41:16 systemd-logind: Power key pressed short.        <-- second press needed\n       host back up 02:43,  `uptime` = 0 min,  EC2 status checks ok throughout\n```\n\nAn ACPI power-button event (an EC2 API reboot), not an OOM or panic. Note the shutdown itself\n**hung** and required a second press — consistent with the loaded host, and worth remembering as a\nsymptom to expect during future maintenance.\n\nDuring the window Gerrit was fully unreachable at TCP level (`HTTP=000`, connect timeout at 45s and\n100s; `git ls-remote` killed at 90s). It recovered on its own: root now answers **HTTP 200 in 0.50s**\nand `ls-remote` returns in **2s**.\n\n### Two incidental findings from the same logs\n\n1. **Probe truncation confirmed from the host's own mouth**, corroborating the metric-side analysis:\n   `rebar-health: probe exit report: SERVICE_RESULT=timeout EXIT_CODE=killed EXIT_STATUS=TERM\n   probe_truncated=1`.\n2. **A duplicate `Change-Id` is breaking the review bot for one change.** Its reconcile loop logs:\n   `HTTP 404: Multiple changes found for I266870f28c4935ad009ceff3d9c32479cb2c7988`. That is the\n   failure mode `git commit --amend -m/-F` produces (it drops the trailer, the hook stamps a fresh\n   one, and a duplicate change opens). The bot cannot resolve the id, so it cannot vote on that\n   change — worth its own ticket if it is not already tracked.\n\n### Suggested direction (not a decision)\n\n`unless-stopped` -> `always` for review-bot would fix the specific gap, but on its own it converts a\nsilent outage into a possible crash loop, so it needs pairing with an actual liveness check on the\n*vote-casting capability* rather than on the process. The deeper issue this ticket already names is\nthat autodeploy reported \"up to date\" while the service was down: a deploy check that inspects\ndesired-vs-actual image state, and not whether the container is running and voting, will keep\nreporting green through exactly this failure.","timestamp":1788662864776870001}],"created_at":1788654045640987001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Summary\n\n`rebar-autodeploy` reports `\"up to date; no-op\"` while declared services are DEAD. On 2026-09-05 the\n`review-bot` and `opcert` containers exited at a host power cycle and stayed down for **24 minutes**\nacross at least twelve autodeploy runs, every one of which logged success.\n\n`LLM-Review` votes stopped landing for every session during that window. Nothing detected it; it was\nfound by hand while investigating why three changes sat at `Verified +1` with no LLM vote.\n\n## Observed\n\n```\ndocker ps -a\n  rebar-mcp-1d60c5f72ff0-8092   Up 20 minutes (healthy)\n  compose-gerrit-1              Up 22 minutes\n  compose-review-bot-1          Exited (127) 24 minutes ago     <-- DOWN\n  compose-opcert-1              Exited (127) 24 minutes ago     <-- DOWN\n\njournalctl -u rebar-autodeploy (runs every ~2 min, exit 0 each time)\n  {\"event\":\"autodeploy\",\"msg\":\"mcp reconcile: swept orphan mcp images (removed=0 kept-live+prev=1)\"}\n  {\"event\":\"autodeploy\",\"msg\":\"up to date (1d60c5f72ff008ddc3acdff42fd5b84ecdfb2752); no-op\"}\n```\n\nRecovery was a manual `docker start compose-review-bot-1 compose-opcert-1`; both came back\nimmediately and the bot resumed accepting webhooks (`POST /webhook 202`, `GET /health 200`).\n\n## The defect\n\nAutodeploy's liveness question is **\"is the deployed SHA current?\"**, not **\"are the declared\nservices running?\"**. Those diverge exactly when it matters. It also reconciles only the `mcp`\nimage — `review-bot` and `opcert` have no reconcile path at all, so nothing was even looking.\n\nThis is the session's recurring shape: a check that runs, reports success, and is silent about the\nproperty it exists to protect. Siblings: `erratic-sunny-genet` (Mirror Guard reports\n`healthy:false` when it could not reach the host), `deistic-conventual-blackmamba` (CI votes\n`Verified-1 FAILURE` on a cancelled run), `satirical-baryte-cat` (worktree GC hangs inside its own\nlock and every later run SKIPs).\n\n## Why it matters for stability specifically\n\nThe system's three services are Gerrit, the rebar MCP server, and the code-review bot. Two of the\nthree can be down indefinitely with the deploy mechanism reporting healthy. No alarm covers this:\nthe review bot has no liveness metric, so its absence is not a missing-data condition either — it\nis simply invisible.\n\n## Note on exit 127\n\nBoth containers exited **127**. The logs before death show the review bot failing to clone from the\nGerrit it SHARES A HOST WITH (`RPC failed; curl 28 Operation too slow. Less than 1000 bytes/sec`)\nand a tracker write timing out under lock contention. Whether 127 is an ungraceful-termination\nartifact of the power cycle or a genuine entrypoint fault is NOT established — worth determining,\nbecause those need different fixes.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 Autodeploy detects a declared-but-not-running service and says so, distinctly from a\n      SHA-currency no-op.\n- [ ] AC2 It either restarts such a service or fails loudly. Decide and RECORD which; silently\n      restarting a container that is crash-looping is its own failure mode.\n- [ ] AC3 `review-bot` and `opcert` have a reconcile path, or a recorded reason they do not.\n- [ ] AC4 A liveness signal exists for the review bot such that its absence is detectable — today\n      it is invisible rather than merely unmeasured.\n- [ ] AC5 Both branches proven: a healthy deployment still no-ops quietly; a dead service is\n      reported.\n\n## Constraints\n\nNever use `--force` or any gate bypass. `timeout` does not exist on this macOS host (exit 127) —\nbound with `perl -e 'alarm N; exec @ARGV'`. Terraform apply is operator-authorized and must follow a\nreviewed plan. Do not touch the shared main checkout; do not `git stash`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","0480-df66-b3df-4aee"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0480-df66-b3df-4aee","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"5ee6-5523-2a12-46e0","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Autodeploy reports 'up to date' while review-bot and opcert are dead: 24min silent LLM-Review outage","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["34dda3c2-28d3-4c4f-9d85-d1ac137e9511","3e3d48a6-51e3-420d-b082-f247e88c7fc3"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788666228816165001,"uuid":"8234c7b6-0cca-4844-a44d-4a9ba67cc18e"}